  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 310 AM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nShowers continue Saturday night through Sunday as the upper low \nmoves slowly eastward. As a result, multiple rounds of light to \nmoderate showers can be generally expected during this timeframe. \nContinued overcast and rainy conditions keep high temperatures in \nthe 50s to low 60s for most locations. Guidance has the upper low \neventually exiting the region by Monday afternoon. Lingering \nactivity may occur across the Lower Trans Pecos with lift occurring \non the backside of the low, however most areas will be dry. \n\nModels continue to show a split jet pattern early to middle part of \nnext week. This pattern will prevent cold Canadian air from \nfiltering into the region and keeping temperatures near-normal \nfor this time of year (mid 60s to mid 70s). Some guidance depicts \na few upper-level disturbances moving across the region. These \ncould bring low (10-30%) rain chances back into the forecast, \nthough no significant weather impacts are expected under this \npattern. Lows also look to remain above normal (40s to low 50s) \nwhich will prolong the first frost date for many areas in the \nmeantime. \n\nLamberson",
